ere and it's so great to be  home I'm working partly out of the  apartment because I've got plenty of  space now as opposed to the place that  we were living in before we probably now  have I would say close to four times the  space that we were working with  previously and we've got a great kitchen  setup you know the bathrooms are all set  up the office not quite so much there's  about 90 boxes of books to be unloaded  you see those those Tim that lumber  behind me that's supposed to be a  bookshelf that's a bookshelf in potentia  that I'm going to have to create later  on today with you know basically just  screwing things together but I've got to  make quite a few more those towels our  library but it's this is really great  we've got plenty of room I've got a  place upstairs where I can I can shoot  videos and I've already started shooting  some for the half-hour Hagel I'm working  out of a collaborative office space  downtown actually the third ward if you  know where that is in Milwaukee called  the Hudson business lounge I think it's  called that because there's also a cafe  right next to called the Hudson so that  is the really big information a bit  really big event if you like it took  several days of pretty intense stuff to  get here I already shot a video about  that so I don't need to tell you those  stories again I will say this i am  extraordinarily happy to be here it was  good to be in New York it was a great  experience but there's nothing like  coming home so what else October saw the  American Catholic philosophical  association in which I gave two papers  both in Satellite sessions one was in  the International hdangel soul society  and I gave a paper there on 18 jul saw  Christian philosophy his model of it and  whether Kierkegaard's philosophical  fragments would fit into that you can  see the link below that if you're  interested in hearing the talk or  reading it you can you can get it  through that I also by invitation gave a  paper at the